  "name": "vector_light_shader_max_gap",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "\u00a727 phase 6 on an open GAP rather than an open door: the same midnight room and torch, with the east wall's one-cell hole left empty. The door scene confounds two things at once, because RimWorld's glow grid never learns a door opened so vanilla delivers literally nothing beyond one; here vanilla's flood passes the hole and both models light the far side, which leaves only the question the shader is actually being asked -- can it draw a beam SHAPED like the visibility polygon. Same seven arms as vector_light_shader_max.json, and directly comparable to it.",
